  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Firoz Qureshi vs State Of Chhattisgarh on 17 September, 2024 1/6 2024:Cghc:36207 High Court Of Chhattisgarh At Bilaspur Wpc No. 2410 of 2022 Digitally Firoz Qureshi S/o Mohammad Arif, Aged About 36 Years R/o Ward No. 9, signed by Praveen Kurmipara, Balod, District Balod Chhattisgarh. Kumar Sinha ---- Petitio Date: 2024.09.23 10:43:29 +0530 versus 1 - State Of Chhattisgarh Through The Secretary, Department Of Revenue, Mahanadi Bhawan, Atal Nagar, Naya Raipur, District Raipur Chhattisgarh. 2 - The Collector, Balod, District Balod Chhattisgarh. 3 - The Sub -Divisional Officer (Revenue), Balod, District Balod Chhattisga 4 - The Tahsildar, Balod, District Balod Chhattisgarh. 5 - Nagar Palika Parishad, Balod, Through Chief Municipal Officer, Balod District Balod Chhattisgarh. 6 - Dr. Smt. Charu Smita Verma, (Died And Deleted) Through Lrs. As Per Honble Court Order Dated 13-08-02024. 6 (a) Prem Shankar Shrivastav S/o Late Johri Lal Shrivastav, Aged About 75 Years R/o Ward No.19, Lohara Road, Near Railway Fatak, Balod, District- Balod (C.G.) ---- Respondent For Petitioner : Mr. Punit Ruparel, Advocate For Resp. No.1 to 4/ State : Mr. Ajay Pandey, Govt. Advocate For Respondent No.5 : Mr. Anshuman Shrivastava, Advocate For Respondent No.6(a) : Mr. Aman Upadhyay, Advocate Firoz Qureshi vs State Of Chhattisgarh on 17 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/105611053/ 1 S.B.: Hon'ble Shri Parth Prateem Sahu, Judge Order on Board 17/09/2024 1.",
    "facts": "2. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that petitioner after purchase of land, constructed a shop and after obtaining the prior permission, licence and NOC, started business of chicken center. Based on the complaint lodged by respondent No.6, respondent No.5 has taken action against the petitioner and has issued notice for shifting the chicken center to some other place or area and has further mentioned that if petitioner does not shift the chicken center, administration will initiate proceeding of shifting the chicken center, last notice was issued on 09.05.2022. Action on the part of respondent is per se illegal and arbitrary when petitioner is running chicken center after obtaining the prior permission and licence from the competent authority i.e. Registration Certificate from the Govt. of Chhattisgarh Health and Family Welfare Department Food Safety and Standards Authority of India, No Objection Certificate from respondent No.5 and no objection from other nearby residents. When once the petitioner has obtained prior permission, NOC/registration to run chicken center, respondent No.5 erred in issuing notice for removing the chicken center of the petitioner by which he is earning livelihood for himself and for his family members. Issuance of notice is in violation of Article 19 of the Constitution of India. As on the date, petitioner is not possessing any licence/registration certificate, he cannot operate the chicken center legally. He also contended that when the officer of the State administration went to shop of the petitioner to see the same, petitioner has given undertaking that he will shift the shop within a period of one month. Petitioner is still running the shop pursuant to interim order dated 26.05.2022 passed in his favour. 4. Learned counsel for respondent No.6 also opposes the submission of learned counsel for the petitioner and would submit that petitioner is running business of chicken center and selling meat of chicken in residential area. However, after receipt of complaint, respondent No.5 issued letter to the petitioner for shifting of shop which was not complied with.",
    "arguments": "3. Learned counsel for respondent No.5 opposes the submission of learned counsel for the petitioner and would submit that the petitioner purchased the land which is registered as residential land in the revenue record. He also contended that in the copy of sale deed, under the heading \"declaration deed/affidavit\" petitioner has mentioned that land is being purchased for residential purpose."
  },
